{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792891808,"nonce":"MUMTOumUzGwtbDIrRDOVk3aAyQQ=","message":"Landed: the cascade followed each pseudo-class state of an element with a Watch on a signal, and read every watched state through the lazy signal, which made it (so the lazy Interaction signals of 33de4ec were undone for any styled element). Interaction now has onStateChange and stateNamed (a read that makes no signal); NativeCascade keeps one listener per node and no watch for hover, active, focus, focus-visible, focus-within, checked, indeterminate and disabled; form states keep their signals. Per 1,000 Ghost buttons: Watch and SignalBool gone from the census, external charge 99 to 82 MB, live pointer heap 15.8 to 13.2 MB. Remaining and not in Haxe: the first style pass of an element that matches the component library's sheet costs about 66 KB of external charge and about 30 KB of real footprint (a bare Library.part('ui-card'); a classed div with no library sheet costs 0.2 MB per 1,000), so the native CSS engine keeps that per matched element. Also still per button: 1 CssTransition with 9 Transition children (about 0.6 KB live).","files":null}]}